{
  "schema": "laya-executor-admission-transport-rtl-input-v1",
  "scope": "Finite FIRST-only 16x512-bit LAD1 ingress and original receipt through two actual depth2 FIFOs, bounded complete 8192-bit collector, and the existing managed laya_generated_provenance_axi_portal_v1 full validator/owner install for STATE0. The exclusive actual executor A producer lane owns its sole frame at the first real FIFO write; the producer emits only after real LYRQ/LYMP admission. Wrapper integration must route that exclusive lane; no new validation bool or receipt-dependent admission_valid is introduced. Only actual complete valid/ready/accepted authorizes echo. Real FIFO ingress writes/pops, portal handshakes/accepts, and receipt writes/reads are independently counted. Ready-only rejection retains the original A and isolates; a second A is always blocked. Cancel before first write blocks new ingress, cancel after first write completes the old collection, and cancel/live physical changes after acceptance preserve the exact original echo until all 16 actual reads. Tail2/tail1 waits12, blocked portal stability, malformed reserved bytes, absent STATE0, physical epoch/address/capacity mismatch, and persistent cancel before acceptance are finite reset-separated diagnostics. Offline actual C++ executor A and independent literal from a verified host PASS are frozen and whole-byte compared. The source/receipt peer is TB; physical STATE0 configuration, adapter idle, and no-work inputs are controlled. No local validator clone, generated executor same-runtime, full 13BO mapping, source protection, business retirement, physical request closure, CLOSED/REARM/second request, complete model/graph, arithmetic, resource/timing or board claim.",
